Third-party software in the binaries
------------------------------------

The remotesigner and remotesigner-consensus binaries link the Go standard
library and the Go modules below. remotesigner also links the modules listed
under "Linked by remotesigner only": the SDKs of the AWS Secrets Manager,
Azure Key Vault and GCP Secret Manager secret stores and the modules they
bring in, which remotesigner-consensus does not link.
github.com/prometheus/procfs is not linked on Windows or macOS. Each entry
gives the copyright notice of the component, as its source states it, and its
licence. LICENSES/ holds the generic texts of these licences (Apache-2.0.txt,
MIT.txt, BSD-2-Clause.txt, BSD-3-Clause.txt). Each component's exact licence,
with its own copyright notice and wording, is the LICENSE file in its source
at the version recorded in go.sum; release archives and images carry those
files, and the components' NOTICE files, in third_party_licenses/.

The binaries also compile internal/keys/keystore/qrlv1/, a copy of the QRL
keystore v1 implementation (go-qrl-wallet-encryptor-keystore, from
https://github.com/theQRL/qrysm), Copyright (c) 2023 The Quantum Resistant
Ledger, licensed under the MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt), modified by The
go-remotesigner Authors. That implementation includes code derived from
go-eth2-wallet-encryptor-keystorev4
(https://github.com/wealdtech/go-eth2-wallet-encryptor-keystorev4),
Copyright © 2019 - 2023 Weald Technology Trading, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). third_party/qrl-keystore/
holds the original.

